# ND-120 FPGA - local paths. Copy this file to Verilog/fpga/local.mk (which is
# gitignored) and fill in the values for your machine. Nothing here is
# committed with a real path: the checked-in scripts only name the variables.
#
# Who reads it:
#   * every board Makefile, through Verilog/fpga/paths.mk, which exports the
#     values (and lists them in WSLENV, so Windows tools started from WSL see
#     them);
#   * the PowerShell scripts, through Verilog/fpga/paths.ps1;
#   * the Basys3 Tcl scripts, through Verilog/fpga/basys3/paths.tcl;
#   * Verilog/fpga/nexys4ddr/run_board_test.sh.
# The scripts read plain "NAME := value" lines only - no make functions or
# $(...) in a value. A value already set in the environment wins when a
# script is run by hand; under make, local.mk wins over the environment and
# the make command line wins over both.
#
# Paths to Windows tools are Windows paths (backslashes are fine). Leave a
# line commented out to use the fallback given for it.

# Vivado launcher (vivado.bat). Unset = vivado / vivado.bat on the Windows PATH.
# ND120_VIVADO := <Vivado install>\bin\vivado.bat

# Vivado licence file list, handed to Vivado as XILINXD_LICENSE_FILE when that
# is not already set. Several files are separated by ';'.
# Unset = the Windows user (then machine) XILINXD_LICENSE_FILE.
# ND120_VIVADO_LICENSE := <licence file>;<another licence file>

# Gowin EDA gw_sh.exe (Tang Nano 20K backup flow, gowin_build.ps1).
# Unset = gw_sh.exe on the Windows PATH.
# ND120_GOWIN := <Gowin install>\IDE\bin\gw_sh.exe

# Quartus bin folder. No script under Verilog/fpga reads it today (the MiSTer
# build runs Quartus in Docker); the name is fixed here so a future script
# uses this one.
# ND120_QUARTUS := <Quartus install>\bin64

# oss-cad-suite folder on Windows (holds environment.bat), used by
# Verilog/ND-120-Yosys/synh.bat - which reads it from the environment only.
# Unset = yosys on PATH. (The WSL/Linux Tang flow uses OSS_CAD instead,
# default ~/oss-cad-suite.)
# ND120_OSS_CAD := <oss-cad-suite folder>

# Basys3 Vivado GUI project: the folder that holds ND3202D.xpr. REQUIRED for
# every Basys3 script (build, flash, ILA, timing experiments); they stop with
# an error when it is unset.
# ND120_BASYS3_PROJECT := <folder holding ND3202D.xpr>

# Folder holding the other ND repositories (nd120uc, ND110Compile, ...), side
# by side. No script under Verilog/fpga reads it today; the name is fixed
# here so any script that needs a sibling repository uses this one.
# ND_REPOS := <folder holding the ND repositories>
